  <h2>Installation</h2>

  <p>Install the CLI — a single self-contained binary with embedded docs:</p>

  <pre><code>go install github.com/DTRules/DTRules/cmd/dtrules@v1.16.0</code></pre>

  <p>
    Prebuilt binaries for Linux, macOS, and Windows are also on
    <a href="https://github.com/DTRules/DTRules/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Releases</a>.
    See <a href="/downloads">Downloads</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the CLI</h2>

  <pre><code># Build a project (Excel → XML, compile DSL → postfix)
dtrules build

# Verify Excel ↔ XML consistency and references
dtrules verify

# Run a decision table (batch)
dtrules run --entry Compute_Eligibility

# Run as an interactive interview (prompts for collect fields)
dtrules run --interactive

# Or serve the same interview in the browser
dtrules run --web</code></pre>

  <p>
    See <a href="/interview">the interactive interview</a> for how
    <code>--interactive</code> and <code>--web</code> turn a decision table into a conversation.
  </p>

  <h2>Using as a Library</h2>

  <pre><code>package main

import (
    "os"
    "github.com/DTRules/DTRules/pkg/dtrules/session"
)

func main() &#123;
    // Create a rule set
    rs := session.NewRuleSet("MyRules")

    // Load EDD (Entity Data Dictionary)
    eddFile, _ := os.Open("EDD.xml")
    rs.LoadEDD(eddFile)
    eddFile.Close()

    // Load Decision Tables
    dtFile, _ := os.Open("DecisionTables.xml")
    rs.LoadDecisionTables(dtFile)
    dtFile.Close()

    // Create a session and execute
    sess, _ := rs.NewSession()
    rsess := sess.(*session.RSession)
    rsess.Execute("Compute_Eligibility")
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2>Architecture</h2>

  <p>DTRules uses a three-stack interpreter similar to PostScript:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Data Stack</strong>: Holds operands and intermediate values</li>
    <li><strong>Entity Stack</strong>: Provides scoped dictionary lookup (context)</li>
    <li><strong>Control Stack</strong>: Manages stack frames and local variables</li>
  </ul>

  <pre><code>┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              DTRules Runtime                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Expression → Compiler → Executable Code    │
│                              │              │
│              ┌───────────────┼───────────┐  │
│              ▼               ▼           │  │
│       ┌───────────┐   ┌───────────┐      │  │
│       │  Object   │   │   Value   │      │  │
│       │   Stack   │   │   Stack   │      │  │
│       └───────────┘   └───────────┘      │  │
│              │               │           │  │
│              └───────┬───────┘           │  │
│                      ▼                   │  │
│               ┌───────────┐              │  │
│               │  Entity   │              │  │
│               │   Stack   │              │  │
│               └───────────┘              │  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>

  <h2>Package Structure</h2>

  <pre><code>DTRules/
├── cmd/
│   ├── dtrules/          # CLI tool (single self-contained binary)
│   ├── api/              # REST API server for UI
│   └── sinusitis-web/    # Embedded-rules web demo (//go:embed)
└── pkg/dtrules/
    ├── compiler/         # Postfix expression compiler
    ├── interpreter/      # State and bytecode VM
    ├── operators/        # 330+ built-in operators
    ├── session/          # Session and RuleSet management
    ├── decisiontable/    # Decision table execution
    ├── authoring/        # Typed authoring view + Project API
    ├── web/              # Web interview server
    └── benchmark/        # Performance benchmarks</code></pre>

